q1["rec"] = {"option": "A", "why": "Your Q4 answer says nobody will be held to this, and the one-page policy statement in B existed only to make the guide required practice. Without enforcement, B adds a page and a signer for nothing. A is what draft v1 already is, and it matches leadership's 7/30 preference. The cost, stated plainly: a guide no one is held to only changes behaviour where the forms (consent, vendor addendum, offboarding) get built into existing steps, which is round 3's question about what 'in use' means."}
q1["thread"].append({"who": "agent", "text": "Reopened because of your Q4 note: \"I don't see this being something that will be required practice... no one's going to be really held to them specifically.\" Confirm A, or keep B if you still want the statement for show.", "at": now})

